ical tubes, precision steel components, and billets that are used in gears, hubs, axles, crankshafts and motor shafts, oil country drill pipes, bits and collars, bearing races and rolling elements, bushings, fuel injectors, wind energy shafts, anti-friction bearings, artillery and mortar bodies, and other applications. The company also offers customized precision steel components. It offers its products and services to the automotive, energy, industrial equipment, mining, construction, rail, aerospace and defense, heavy truck, agriculture, and power generation sectors. The company was formerly known as TimkenSteel Corporation and changed its name to Metallus Inc. in February 2024. Metallus Inc. was founded in 1899 and is headquartered in Canton, Ohio.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Michael S. Williams B.Sc. | CEO & Director | Age 65 | Compensation: $2.0M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $610K ranks in the below the sector median among Basic Materials peers. Stock-based compensation of $8K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 3\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["Metallus Inc. is a small-cap basic materials business with a $699M market cap on $1.2B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -5% over the past three years and +0% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at 14% against a 11% cost of capital, a 4-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it, and 8% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The company is burning through $93M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage of 36\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield is only 1.9%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 14% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Operating margins 9% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 6.4% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are overwhelmingly selling (86% sell ratio) \u2014 the people who know the business want less of it","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","ratio":0.143},{"text":"Gross margin trails most Basic Materials peers \u2014 competitors appear to have the pricing hand","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Trade policy and tariff whiplash \u2014 materials producers are first-order casualties of protectionist swings, and margin gets squeezed from both input and output pricing.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Shares offer a 23% margin of safety against estimated fair value","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Among the least levered in Basic Materials \u2014 the fortress balance sheet in its peer set"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Timken declares $0.36 dividend","source":"seekingalpha.com","link":"https://seekingalpha.com/news/4672415-timken-declares-0_36-dividend","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794581421.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.296,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":["dividend"]},{"title":"Timken Declares Quarterly Dividend of 36 Cents Per Share","source":"prnewswire.com","link":"https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/timken-declares-quarterly-dividend-of-36-cents-per-share-302939005.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794581100.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.494,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings","dividend"]},{"title":"Timken (TKR) Just Raised A Bigger Question","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/capital-goods/nyse-tkr/timken/news/timken-tkr-just-raised-a-bigger-question","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794579316.614,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.796,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Timken Earns Recognition on Forbes America's Best Companies 2027 List","source":"prnewswire.com","link":"https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/timken-earns-recognition-on-forbes-americas-best-companies-2027-list-302938051.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794499200.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.735,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Does Raised Guidance Change The Bull Case For Timken Stock (TKR)?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/capital-goods/nyse-tkr/timken/news/does-raised-guidance-change-the-bull-case-for-timken-stock-t","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794489909.261,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.875,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":["guidance"]},{"title":"US humanoid robot production could hit 400,000 by 2030 as deployment ramps, J.P. Morgan says","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/us-humanoid-robot-production-could-094852000.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestam